       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is unsafe as written.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the maximum prescription dose of 3,200 mg/day. At that level the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot.\n\nHere are some common regimens you might have meant:\n- **400 mg PO four times daily:** 1,600 mg/day. This is a typical dose for mild to moderate pain or inflammation.\n- **600 mg PO four times daily:** 2,400 mg/day.\n- **800 mg PO three times daily:** 2,400 mg/day. This is a common dose for musculoskeletal pain or arthritis.\n- **800 mg PO four times daily:** 3,200 mg/day. This is the maximum, and it is generally used only short-term.\n\nTell me which dose and frequency you want, or confirm the indication, and I'll enter it. Check the plan with your resident or attending as well. I can add a note to the order, such as \"take with food.\""
