     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the problem. 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of 3,200 mg, and a normal-looking kidney and liver profile doesn't make that safe. At that dose the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events goes up, and there's no added pain relief. Analgesic and anti-inflammatory effects plateau well below it.\n\nYou have a few ways forward:\n- **Enter a dose within the limit.** I can do that right now, for example 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day) or 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum). Tell me which one.\n- **Talk to your resident or attending.** If you think this dose is intended, for example for a specific protocol, they should review it and enter or co-sign it. Pharmacy will probably flag it anyway.\n- **Tell me the clinical goal.** If the pain control isn't adequate, there may be better options, such as scheduled acetaminophen alongside the NSAID or a different drug class.\n\nTell me how you'd like to proceed."
      }
     ],
